# Line-ending policy
#
# The Driver Automation Tool is a Windows-only product and the SHA256 values in
# "Driver Automation Tool/FileHashes.md" are generated from the checked-out
# working copy. Without an explicit policy the checked-out bytes depend on each
# user's core.autocrlf setting, so the published hashes could not be verified
# reliably. Pinning the source files to CRLF makes every clone byte-identical.

*.ps1    text eol=crlf
*.psm1   text eol=crlf
*.psd1   text eol=crlf
*.xaml   text eol=crlf
*.config text eol=crlf

# Catalog payloads are generated/downloaded data that is already stored with
# CRLF. Opt them out of normalisation so they are never silently rewritten.
Data/*.json -text
Data/*.xml  -text
